{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy","id":758179,"title":"Fields for the Technocracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-06T01:13:40-08:00","id":758179,"title":"Fields for the Technocracy","content":"This hack provides an alternative to the Spheres for the Technocracy's use. It borrows some key concepts from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, though probably not in the way one might expect. It is also very much a Work In Progress, and I would very much like constructive feedback on it. (Kudos to Ajax, who has already provided considerable feedback.)<br /> <br /> <u>First Draft</u><br /> Under this setup, the Union uses a set of twelve Fields of study, loosely organized into three groups of four:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Dimension<br /> \u2022 Foundation<br /> \u2022 Space<br /> \u2022 Time<br /> <br /> \u2022 Ephemera<br /> \u2022 Forces<br /> \u2022 Life<br /> \u2022 Matter<br /> <br /> \u2022 Data<br /> \u2022 Fortune<br /> \u2022 Mind<br /> \u2022 Utility<br /> <br /> The <i>Dimension</i> and <i>Ephemera</i> Fields deal with what the Spirit Sphere does: Dimension deals with crossing into the Umbrae and navigating once you get there; Ephemera deals with ectoplasm, ghosts, spirits, and similar phenomena. I might decide to fold these Fields back together; but my gut instinct is to treat them as separate Fields. <br /> <br /> <i>Data</i> and <i>Space</i> both originated from what the Traditions call Correspondence, but have developed into distinct things; they are not considered to be variants of a common Field, but are treated as two separate Fields. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Space is the most like Correspondence, in that it includes the ability to influence position and motion (including, in a nod to Einstein, control over gravity); but its influence over Sympathetic connections is seriously restricted: it can still do stunts like teleportation and collocation with suitable spatial connections; but said connections rarely occur naturally and usually have to be manufactured, and manufacturing them usually requires proximity. Typically, a quantum entanglement or stable wormhole is established in close proximity and then the end points are separated for future use. Alternatively, conjunctional use of Data can use a Data connection to bypass the need for close proximity. Which brings us to:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Data cannot manipulate position or motion; it does not include teleportation, collocation, or warping space in any way. However, it's very good at establishing connections as long as there's network access to the subject. It's also capable of accessing the Digital Web (something Space <i>can't</i> do at all), and is capable of influencing digital machines and entities in a matter similar to what Mind can do with people. This includes reading, influencing, or disrupting \u201cthought processes\u201d, messing with memory, and reading or spoofing sensors. <br /> <br /> <i>Foundation</i> and <i>Utility</i> were once called \u201cPrimal Energy\u201d and \u201cPrimal Utility\u201d, respectively. There's a <i>lot</i> of overlap here as things stand, with the main difference being that Utility has access to Primal Ventures and is slightly better at crafting Wonders while Primal Energy has an edge where Nodes and Tass are concerned. I'm still thinking this one through to see if I can make the two more distinct, and even whether or not I want Foundation as a distinct Field <i>at all</i>. I think Foundation could be ditched by making the things that it can do that don't fit Utility's concept into conjunctional effects (e.g., Nodes become Space/Utility or Dimension/Utility; Junctions become Time/Utility; Tass becomes Matter/Utility), or folding them directly into Spheres that Scientists with a more materialistic bent are likely to take (see my notes further on about Matter and technological Wonders). <br /> <br /> At present, <i>Fortune</i> is a straight renaming of Entropy, but with a stronger emphasis on influencing fate, destiny, and luck. Decay-related stuff is more a matter of dealing with Entropic Resonance, and is more properly a function of Prime-like Fields. I'm considering the possibility of dropping Fortune as well, with its fate/destiny/luck functionality folding into Time. <br /> <br /> The Field of <i>Matter</i> puts more emphasis on machinery than its Sphere counterpart, though it retains the ability to mess with material properties. It <i>might</i> extend that focus on machinery into the realm of messing with technological Wonders, depending on what I end up doing with Foundation and Utility. <br /> <br /> At present, I'm treating the Fields of <i>Forces</i>, <i>Life</i>, <i>Mind</i>, and <i>Time</i> exactly like their counterpart Spheres. if anything, I might end up tweaking the Forces and Life Spheres to be more mystical in feel; but that's a subject for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/88705-sphere-variants-for-the-traditions\">another thread</a>. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> There are a number of cases here where several Fields overlap or do very similar things; this is a feature, not a bug. When it happens, my intention is \u201cfactor out\u201d the overlapping or similar Effects into a separate \u201cClass\u201d of Effects, and to reference that class in the appropriate Fields instead of listing the individual Effects multiple times. Examples where such classes might be appropriate include: Data and Mind have similar \u201ccognition\u201d Effects, differing primarily in terms of whether you're dealing with a sapient's cognitive processes or \u201cdigital cognition\u201d; Matter lets you influence machinery in a manner similar to how Life lets you influence the behavior of animals and how Ephemera lets you influence spirits; Data provides access to the Digital Web in a manner similar to how Dimension lets you access the Umbrae; Data and Space have similar Effects when it comes to connectivity. And so on. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T02:03:49-08:00","id":758298,"title":"","content":"I think, in general, it seems pretty solid as an alternate set of fields.<br /> <br /> My main concerns are a mix of thematic and practical.<br /> <br /> On the thematic side, it seems like you could shuffle things around a bit to make these align more with the &quot;ideal&quot; Technocratic paradigm. As you noted, Fortune doesn't really seem to fit. But why have Dimension, Space, and Ephemera? Dimension seems like it should just be accomplished by mixing Space and Ephemera. If you wanted to keep three categories of equal numbers, what about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Foundation<br /> \u2022 Space<br /> \u2022 Time<br /> <br /> \u2022 Forces<br /> \u2022 Life<br /> \u2022 Matter<br /> <br /> \u2022 Data<br /> \u2022 Mind<br /> \u2022 Utility<br /> <br /> You can make Foundation more distinct from Utility by folding Ephemera into it. This essentially creates the idea that alternate dimensional entities (aka spirits) aren't some inherently separate form of being. A canid formed extra-dimensional being is still a Life Pattern. However these alternate dimensions seem to be infused with Primal Energy making manipulations of those dimensions, the entities within them, and the connection points between our dimension and those (links to the idea that Foundation deals with Nodes and Tass), to an extent that requires significant knowledge of Foundation to adequately interact with them.<br /> <br /> I kind of really like that idea that the Technocracy doesn't interact with &quot;spirits,&quot; and can fully justify their stance that these extra-dimensional beings aren't anything of the sort. Rather the extremely high levels of Primal Energy present there unregulated results in wildly distorted pockets of space influenced either by the unknowing masses, or by Reality Deviants tapping into those reserves to create perverse &quot;playgrounds.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the practical side of things, I'm curious how you see this interacting with Tradition mages. How do countermagic effects line up when the rules assume everyone uses the same Spheres (even if renamed)? What happens if a Technocrat defects to a Tradition? Or a mystic to the Union? Etc. Have mages essential come full circle to the point where the Union's magic is like a one Dark Ages Fellowship's magic and the mystics are using a different Fellowship, and even the idea of compatibility has been lost? Or is this are purely mechanical separation but things are meant to stay the same in-universe in terms of how the mystic groups and Technocrats are meant to interact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T05:45:01-08:00","id":758465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy#post758179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At present, <i>Fortune</i> is a straight renaming of Entropy, but with a stronger emphasis on influencing fate, destiny, and luck. Decay-related stuff is more a matter of dealing with Entropic Resonance, and is more properly a function of Prime-like Fields. I'm considering the possibility of dropping Fortune as well, with its fate/destiny/luck functionality folding into Time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fortune can be replaced with probability which will cover everything Entropy covers from chance to the inevitable like decay. <br /> <br /> On a side note when you split spheres up are your just making the player spend more exp for thing other get normally?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:26:05-08:00","id":758627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=758465#post758465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fortune can be replaced with probability which will cover everything Entropy covers from chance to the inevitable like decay.<br /> <br /> On a side note when you split spheres up are your just making the player spend more exp for thing other get normally?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Probability for a Technocratic version of Entropy as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7061-azrael","name":"Azrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7061_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:28:56-08:00","id":758632,"title":"","content":"FWIW, I chose Fortune as a name with the Syndicate in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:08:19-08:00","id":758669,"title":"","content":"While Fortune does make sense in the Syndicate sense, the overwhelming focus on probability and its resolution makes me think that <i>Stochastics</i> would be a better choice. Partly because it is a term the rest of the Union would have no problem using, and partly because it is just like the Syndicate to think of human behavior as a random element.<br /> <br /> On another note, given the way you've set up these fields to overlap and provide different ways of looking at the same thing, would certain Conventions take penalties to learning certain fields?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:11:37-08:00","id":758672,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with Fortune, or Probability, is that from a Technocratic perspective this isn't a fundamental aspect of reality, but an emergent property of the interactions of components in a complex system. If you want to mess with the probability of something happening, probability science says that you don't change probability itself, you change the properties of the components interacting with each other. For example, if you want ice to melt when the external temperature is below freezing, you don't change the odds of light particles of exciting ice molecules to break apart. You either increase the intensity of the light, increase the ambient heat, or decrease the energy required to melt ice (aka you add salt). In other words, you use Forces or Matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:41:50-08:00","id":758773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=758672#post758672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem with Fortune, or Probability, is that from a Technocratic perspective this isn't a fundamental aspect of reality, but an emergent property of the interactions of components in a complex system. If you want to mess with the probability of something happening, probability science says that you don't change probability itself, you change the properties of the components interacting with each other. For example, if you want ice to melt when the external temperature is below freezing, you don't change the odds of light particles of exciting ice molecules to break apart. You either increase the intensity of the light, increase the ambient heat, or decrease the energy required to melt ice (aka you add salt). In other words, you use Forces or Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life and Mind are both emergent properties from a scientific perspective, yet technocrats still use those spheres. Also, from a super-science perspective Probability might be seen as an aspect of quantum processes that underlie reality, and are able to be manipulated using various devices. Psychic technocrats might also be able to influence probability. Additionally, a technocrat might be able to interact with the environment in &quot;mundane ways&quot; to nudge probability in a particular direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7061-azrael","name":"Azrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7061_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:44:23-08:00","id":758782,"title":"","content":"There's a reason why I had it grouped with Data, Mind, and Utility. And if it gets dropped, the probability manipulation stuff is more likely to go into Time than either Forces or Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:51:05-08:00","id":758788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=758672#post758672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem with Fortune, or Probability, is that from a Technocratic perspective this isn't a fundamental aspect of reality, but an emergent property of the interactions of components in a complex system. If you want to mess with the probability of something happening, probability science says that you don't change probability itself, you change the properties of the components interacting with each other. For example, if you want ice to melt when the external temperature is below freezing, you don't change the odds of light particles of exciting ice molecules to break apart. You either increase the intensity of the light, increase the ambient heat, or decrease the energy required to melt ice (aka you add salt). In other words, you use Forces or Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is to say that's not what Technocrats see themselves doing? Altering the initial conditions of chaotic systems to significantly alter the outcomes? That would fall under the domain of probability. Small changes that butterfly outward might initially be started with forces or matter (or any other field for that matter) but figuring out what changes and when is something else entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:54:23-08:00","id":758800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=758782#post758782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason why I had it grouped with Data, Mind, and Utility. And if it gets dropped, the probability manipulation stuff is more likely to go into Time than either Forces or Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy and Time do blur a bit when you really think about it. I mean if you understand Entropy/Probability you should be a able to predict future events and guess at past events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7061-azrael","name":"Azrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7061_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:55:09-08:00","id":758801,"title":"","content":"On another note, the suggestion about combining Ephemera and Foundation is intriguing; I'll have to think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=758800#post758800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entropy and Time do blur a bit when you really think about it. I mean if you understand Entropy/Probability you should be a able to predict future events and guess at past events.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the matter of the Arrow of Time: while I don't want to get too hung up on the decay aspects of Entropy, a strong case could be made that another word for increasing Entropy is \u201caging\u201d \u2014 something Time ought to be able to accelerate, slow, stop, or even reverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-06-2015, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T10:20:27-08:00","id":758985,"title":"","content":"Ok, I don't want to derail too much in this regard, but I want to push back a little on something:<br /> <br /> Probability, from a scientific perspective, doesn't actually exist. It is a mathematical abstract that tries to predict complex systems that we cannot measure in sufficient detail to know the precise results of inputs into a system. In theory, the chance of everything that does happen is always 1, because if you had perfect knowledge of the system(s) involved, you would be able to determine the exact outcome without any question. Probability is necessary because we are incapable of perfect knowledge, and have to observe complex systems to see how they usually act to extrapolate what the odds are of something happening.<br /> <br /> Putting the majority of Entropy effects in Time is fine. Time could use the boost in low level stuff, and the scientific model of time is covers more of what the Entropy Spheres covers. It doesn't have to be a Matter/Forces/etc. though overlap there is probably something that the system will generate (and the RAW system already does).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T13:11:22-08:00","id":759218,"title":"","content":"Since probability is a mathematical abstraction, and from a comparison-to-the-Spheres perspective Data is the relatively sparse &quot;Correspondence minus space-stuff&quot;, and probability is a matter of &quot;complex interplay of details&quot; in the Technoparadigm... wouldn't it fit to fold most of the fate/fortune aspects of Entropy into Data?<br /> <br /> Then Data can be about relationships and complexity theory. The relationship between symbol and object, between fiddly details and the outcome of events, between actions and consequences, between individuals in an organization and between an individual and the organization they're a member of. It would also serve as a repository for all the associative and 'sympathetic' stuff that's in Correspondence.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate would study Data to predict and influence how their investments will go by examining the interplay of factors that affect them, Iteration X would study it for its interaction with computation and the complexities of use cases between man and machine, the NWO would study it for how societies behave in relation to their members. The Progenitors would study it for bioinformatics and the interplay of ecosystems.<br /> <br /> The deathy-type stuff (what there is) can go in Foundations, when it deals with the Underworld and ghosts, and the Pattern Spheres, when it deals with breaking/fixing Patterns. Scrambling or stabilizing organizations, conceptual entropy, and the like would fall under Data since they're effectively affecting the Pattern of those organizations and relationships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T13:50:08-08:00","id":759294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=759218#post759218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since probability is a mathematical abstraction, and from a comparison-to-the-Spheres perspective Data is the relatively sparse &quot;Correspondence minus space-stuff&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so; it also has the rather extensive \u201cif it's digital, I can mess with it\u201d stuff, which currently is only done via Forces or Matter (I think; from what I hear, <b>Book of Secrets</b> will address how to do computer-related stuff using the Spheres). This is in keeping with the official Data Sphere's reliance on a data network to do Correspondence-like things; Data becomes the Field of \u201call things digital\u201d. It's a Field that really comes into its own in the Information Age, as ubiquitous programming becomes more and more of a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T20:11:58-08:00","id":759663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=758985#post758985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I don't want to derail too much in this regard, but I want to push back a little on something:<br /> <br /> Probability, from a scientific perspective, doesn't actually exist. It is a mathematical abstract that tries to predict complex systems that we cannot measure in sufficient detail to know the precise results of inputs into a system. In theory, the chance of everything that does happen is always 1, because if you had perfect knowledge of the system(s) involved, you would be able to determine the exact outcome without any question. Probability is necessary because we are incapable of perfect knowledge, and have to observe complex systems to see how they usually act to extrapolate what the odds are of something happening.<br /> <br /> Putting the majority of Entropy effects in Time is fine. Time could use the boost in low level stuff, and the scientific model of time is covers more of what the Entropy Spheres covers. It doesn't have to be a Matter/Forces/etc. though overlap there is probably something that the system will generate (and the RAW system already does).</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor quibble: perfect knowledge of the inputs, even when combined with complete knowledge of the physical laws of the universe, does not guarantee perfect prediction of the outcome. You still run into emergent behaviors that you can only determine experimentally by letting the system play out. A perfect simulation of the universe could still work, but that's theoretically impossible even without trying to get it to run faster than the universe itself. <br /> <br /> Second minor quibble: Technocrats are still Mages, and might actually try to manipulate an abstraction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:03:23-08:00","id":760051,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver well knows my feelings about folding in a lot of what is now in Entropy, or at least what is in Entropy that is not just something that crosses over with another Sphere in an almost completely redundant manner that leads to massive Sphere bloat on effects.... E.g. Matter 3 should certainly be able to &quot;break stuff&quot; as, if not more effectively than Entropy 3 and that's the KEY ability of Entropy 3, and the result is all too often to require BOTH Spheres to do something that is redundant in one and necessary in the other. MOST of Entropy as written consists of just such overlaps. What is left can be used to beef up Time and make it more interesting, more usable and a able to do things that are more in line with Time manipulation overall. Time should NOT just be the &quot;ordering&quot; moments. It can, and to my mind, should, definitely embrace issues of causation.<br /> <br /> We're currently playtesting that kind of Time in my chronicle (which is a massively Time-oriented romp). It's not in a &quot;post-ready&quot; format as of yet, but it seems to be working. <br /> <br /> Entropy is pretty much gutted at that point. I've set up something that really should be called something like &quot;Systems&quot; to take it's place and it seems to be working. The two Technocrat players seem to love it. <br /> <br /> I think HA may have a point in the 3 by 3 by 3 system he sets up. Not only does it track the 9 Spheres in an overall &quot;mystic underpinings of the game&quot; sense, but it is parsimonious. Saying EDE's are effectively just Life or Forces with a lot of Prime in them seems like a genius way to handle it. Why not? Different mystic viewpoints seems to allow for perception of the same incident from alternate Spheres/Fields.<br /> <br /> As per previous conversations in other threads (and with Data), I still think there is room for a differentiation between Matter (Materials science) and Machine (Engineering). (We're also playtesting a Machine version of Matter as well. That is mostly post-ready. I need to go through and integrate the new material from M20) However, when I consider it in light of HA and his ideas of how to integrate Fields to cover dealing with EDE's, I think there might be some similar combination of Fields (Forces &amp; Matter leap to mind, but something else might work as well or be added to the mix...)<br /> <br /> I like the Data and Space differentiation a lot. I am already using them as alternate Spheres, with Data pretty much as Data describes (no matter movement, easy access to the Digital Web... that one is pretty much DONE done... I need to put in a side-bar on Augmented Reality.... probably approaching a &quot;fourth vidare&quot; (all credit for that goes directly to Data) and retooling the chart that came with the original Data in the NWO book....). We're running Space off of some notes I wrote down in a very very boring in-service and it is working so far. Space is run off a set of charts on what level (how many dots) are required to access specific functions (it is MUCH harder to aport and teleport with my Space than with Correspondence, but it is pretty easy to send information via Data. Forces lie somewhere in between) and the ways in which to allocate successes to cover distance, proximity, number of &quot;targets&quot;, complexity of desired effect. (We're using Arete+Sphere for casting rolls and dividing successes, so some of my House Rules don't sync with Arete-only mage. It would be WAAAAY harder to get the number of successes to do the things I've described). <br /> <br /> Actually, one character (a time-displaced Analytical Reckoner who seems to have played a part in the VA's defection, though he has amnesia about all that.... he was very upset to find out Turing was dead, but is VERY excited by the Digital Web...) is play-testing this version of Data, Space, Machine AND my new &quot;not-Entropy&quot; Spheres. Seeing what he does with Data/Space interactions has been a lot of fun. Combining Machine with all that has been great. <br /> <br /> I am very curious about the nitty-gritty of how these are different from Spheres. How different in their function? How does the Awakening connection come into play? (Something related to the practices?) What are the mechanics of buying them and allocating them for starting characters?<br /> <br /> Also, I am wondering if some renaming might be in order. The Union might want to separate themselves from the Tradition's &quot;crude&quot; Sphere nomenclature system. Like having Biological Science instead of Life, Psychology for Mind, Material Science for Matter, etc. Maybe there might be an &quot;axis&quot; idea that could work. One axis is the three or four &quot;Sciences&quot; (Material Sciences aka Matter, Biological Science aka Life, Physical Sciences (or something with &quot;Energy&quot; in it for Forces). Another axis could be &quot;Engineering&quot; (Temporal Engineering for Time, Continuum Engineering for Prime, etc.) Maybe Analyses for the others? I dunno. I really like the idea of those three axes. Then each effect could be plotted within a 3-D space as to how much Engineering, Science and Analysis was involved... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T14:12:02-08:00","id":760934,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the shout outs.<br /> <br /> Though I'd push back a bit on the naming thing for a few reasons. First, it's clunky to have to have &quot;sciences&quot; after half of them, but just saying Biology or Psychology, or Materials, wouldn't adequately describe things. I also don't like, even from a Union perspective, as trying to label some fields a science, and another field engineering, and another analysis. Even the Union would acknowledge that the hypertech field of studies encompass all three of those things. The Life Spheres, even as the Field of Life for the Union, is all three of those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T19:47:21-08:00","id":761153,"title":"","content":"On the naming thing: I'm operating on the premise that, as a practical matter, names of broad, general things (such as the Fields) should be short. Note that I reduced Dimensional Science to Dimension, and Primal Utility to Utility. Similarly, my inclination would be to avoid multi-word names for other fields. <br /> <br /> There's a principle in the Perl 6 design community called \u201cHoffman Encoding\u201d which says, in effect, that commonly used things should have short names. The Fields are commonly used, and thus ought to have short names. <br /> <br /> The Fields are also broad in scope, which also suggests concision: usually, adjectives (as well as prefixes and suffixes) get added in when you're narrowing the scope of what you're talking about; and it's counterproductive to <i>start</i> with long names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T11:08:17-08:00","id":761610,"title":"","content":"For the Spheres, I agree with simple one word names. Primal Utility to Utility is okay. Seems like &quot;Value&quot; would be better, since the basic meaning of Utility (usefulness) doesn't really track with the Syndicate's take on the idea of &quot;fundamental/primary/essential [force]&quot; whereas Value is what it's ALL about for them. [Primal] Ventures (Extraordinary? Enlightened? Informed? Advanced) are all about creating value. Economics is all about value. Value and utility don't really have to track at all. <br /> <br /> I have no idea what to call Dimensional Science in a cogent one word that is better than &quot;Dimension&quot; though that seems inadequate and grating....<br /> <br /> Like I said, I need to know the structuring of this idea before I move over. If this is just the Technocratic Spheres (instead of 9, they have X, some of which track, some of which are mix-mastered out of the Tradition's nine), then snappy 1 word names are definitely appropriate needed. If this is a reconceptualization of magic into a new system for the Technocrats (similar but different than the way that the Foundation/Pillar system functions), then one word names might be non-viable. <br /> <br /> Like I said, if there is a 3 axis system, there might 3 names to an effect noting where it is with regard to the concepts of information vs. manipulation vs.... something else I haven't quite put my finger on quite yet. This would be a very different system from the Sphere system. It's an interesting intellectual expermient, but it would probably be too far outside the &quot;mage box&quot; for me to think about putting it into place. (Since M20 fixed whole lot less than I was hoping, I have enough on my hands trying to deal with all the disconnects and clunkiness that was left in place or enhanced in the magic system).<br /> <br /> If the system being proposed is like Awakening in that the Arcana/Spheres/Fields parallel are in place in a way very much like Mage as-is, just with the give and take to orient them out of a fundamentally mystic paradigm/praxis (defining the WHAT is being affected) AND there is also an additional system, a la the Awakening Practices that &quot;overlays&quot; the Fields describing HOW they are being manipulated.... that seems interesting. I would probably grab some of my ideas about the axes and turn them into the &quot;Practice ladders&quot; from Awakening... Like chaining the &quot;Practices&quot; of Adjustment, Modification, Engineering that would track what can be done to the Field in question. (Like the Practices of Weaving and Patterning and Making are successively more powerful iterations of the same concept). This would be particularly interesting if the Practices and Fields were decoupled. Essentially paying XP to gain access to a Field, perhaps at a set base cost (kinda like Foundation) and then buying &quot;Practices&quot; separately (kinda like Pillars but not....) so a Progenitor could the Fields of Biology (Life) and Engineering (Matter with a more mechanical and less alchemical bent) and then have practices that could be applied to both (kinda like having muliple foundations and multiple practices with each practice being able to plug into every Field or combination of Fields).....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:57:54-08:00","id":772678,"title":"","content":"First time poster here. Although I'm still rather new to the franchise I have been reading extensively on the Technocracy. I believe if you wanted to have a more &quot;Technocracy friendly&quot; version of Entropy rather than Fortune or fate or whatever, you might think about calling it &quot;Statistics&quot;. A key concept in statistics is that the larger the n, or sample size, the more predictive the statistic is. In my line of work we like to say that &quot;Big Data is when n=all&quot;. That is, as technology improves and our ability to measure a wider variety of variables increases, our sample size increases to the point where our predictive models are ever more accurate. This seems to fit the technocratic paradigm pretty well; if all variables can be measured accurately, then all events can be extrapolated = static reality is maintained. A technocrat seeking to scry the stars or divine the future or whatever basically seems to be doing statistical analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9798-jdb","name":"JDB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T19:35:45-08:00","id":772733,"title":"","content":"First, welcome to the forums! <br /> <br /> I've been thinking long and hard about this; and I think what you're describing would fit nicely into the Field of Data \u2014 which is looking more and more to be (from the Traditions' perspective) a hybrid of Correspondence and Entropy, plus some Mind-like Procedures for influencing digital processes. It should be all about identifying and manipulating patterns; and that's statistical analysis every bit as much as it's surveillance and records hacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T20:44:31-08:00","id":772768,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> Yes I see what you're saying, thematically it makes more sense for statistics to be incorporated into Data. There's something very appealing to me about a technocrat being able to crunch insane data to basically predict the future or &quot;read minds&quot; (not unlike directed advertisement via search query history) through a combination of statistics and data/correspondence. A fantasy come true for a statshound like myself. Good work and keep it up - sounds intriguing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9798-jdb","name":"JDB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T18:19:14-08:00","id":781990,"title":"","content":"In my first post, I mentioned that one of my inspirations for these Fields is <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>. I didn't go into detail about <i>how</i> <b>Awakening</b> informed my design decisions, because I've been working out the specifics. I still don't have everything nailed down; but here's a taste of what I have in mind:<br /> <br /> With the regular Spheres, each one has a unique progression all its own; to the extent that there's any sort of commonality among the various Spheres' progressions, it's entirely a matter of tendencies and trends. For the Fields, I want to go with a more standardized system akin to <b>Awakening</b>'s Practices. As a first draft of this, I'm borrowing the Capabilities from <b>Mage Translation Guide</b> (page 41) and using them as a framework for defining the Fields:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Field Rank</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><b>Capabilities</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022 <i>Senses:</i> Detect and examine phenomena<br /> \u2022 <i>Self Empowerment:</i> Influence trivial phenomena related to personal capabilities</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022 <i>Minor influence:</i> Command of basic phenomena or the ability to \u201cnudge\u201d phenomena, but not totally control them<br /> \u2022 <i>Trivial Pattern Influence:</i> Certain non-Pattern Spheres may affect Patterns in the most elementary ways. Examples: Enchant weapons, conjure objects from another place</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022 <i>Lesser Pattern Influence:</i> Certain non-Pattern Spheres may target Patterns with minor Effects at this rank (Pattern Spheres may already do so). Examples: teleportation, cursing machinery<br /> \u2022 <i>Minor Transformation:</i> Transform one minor phenomenon into another or with Foundation, manifest it out of nothing<br /> \u2022 <i>Enhance and Repair:</i> Improve phenomena, repair diminished or damaged phenomena</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022 <i>Greater Pattern Influence:</i> Certain non-Pattern Spheres may target Patterns with powerful Effects at this rank (Pattern Spheres may already do so). Examples: Convert matter to ephemera, curse living creatures with disease<br /> \u2022 <i>Major Influence:</i> Complex control over powerful phenomena</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">\u2022 <i>Major Transformation:</i> Convert or reshape powerful phenomena<br /> \u2022 <i>Legendary Influence:</i> Perform a rare or exceptionally powerful feat that is normally not permitted</td> </tr> </table></div> The next step is to cross-reference each Field with these Capabilities, and to decide what each actually <i>means</i>, listing one or more Functions for each that applies (e.g., \u201cLandscape of the Mind\u201d for Space/Senses). I'm working off of the Fields list that Heavy Arms provided on the first page: Foundation, Space, Time; Forces, Life, Matter; Data, Mind, Utility. I won't necessarily be taking them in order, though; and if others want to propose write-ups, I'll welcome the assistance.<br /> <br /> I'm at work right now. But when I'm free, I'll write up a Translation Guide style comparison of the Fields and Spheres to make the task of coming up with Functions a bit easier. <br /> <br /> Note that one of my goals when coming up with Functions is to identify, but not necessarily eliminate, redundancies and near-redundancies. For instance, Foundation will include Functions pertaining to the summoning, binding and warding of EDEs; Life will include Functions pertaining to the summoning, binding, and warding of animals; and Data very well might include Functions to summon, bind, and ward digital entities. I want these Functions to have names that highlight the parallels, with the idea that the mechanics for two of them can eventually be written up along the lines of \u201clike [the third one], but for [X]\u201d \u2014 for instance, \u201clike Summon Animals, but for EDEs\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-07-2015, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T21:10:55-08:00","id":782063,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Foundation:</b> Prime, Spirit</u><br /> Foundation is, almost by definition, the Field of \u201cstuff that's too dangerous for Consensual Reality\u201d, and deals with those things that the Consensus isn't ready for. Its primary proponents are the Void Engineers; and in fact I'm thinking of renaming it as \u201cVoid\u201d (though I'll hold off on doing that until I get some feedback). Prime-like Functions should focus on Tass, Synergy, and Nodes; Spirit-like Functions should focus on the creatures and objects found in the otherworlds. Note that Synergy lets you \u201ctune\u201d your Procedures to different kinds of exotic phenomena; for instance, tuning into Entropic Synergies lets you deal with entropic energies, ghosts, and ectoplasm. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Space:</b> Void Correspondence, Dimensional Science, and Forces</u><br /> The Space Field deals with location and motion. It is also a Void Engineer specialty \u2014 and in fact is that Convention's preferred Field. From Void Correspondence (a minor variation of Correspondence described in the <b>Void Engineers Revised Convention Book</b>) you get proximity-based Procedures; from Dimensional Science, you get manipulation of the Gauntlet and travel beyond Conventional Space (though these Functions might require conjunctional use of Foundation?); from Forces, you get manipulation of motion and gravity. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Time:</b> Time, Entropy</u><br /> Manipulating the flow of time. Can also be used to accelerate, slows halt, or reverse processes, including but not limited to decay. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Forces</b></u><br /> The Field of Forces is likely to be very similar to the Forces Sphere, as I can't think of anything conceptually that warrants changing. Iteration X and the Void Engineers both like this Field. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Life</b></u><br /> The Field of Life is very similar to the Life Sphere. I'm debating the possibility of allowing you to instill hypertechnological mutations into creatures (turning them into living Wonders) without needing to worry about Utility, though Utility should still be more effective at doing so: essentially, Life borrows \u201cliving Wonder\u201d functionality from Prime, while Utility gets its \u201cliving Wonder\u201d functionality from Primal Utility. Needless to say, the Progenitors are the main proponents of this Field. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Matter</b></u><br /> The Field of Matter deals with mechanisms in a manner that parallels how the Field of Life deals with organisms. It also deals with the properties of substances, though it may not be as effective at this as its namesake Sphere is. This is Iteration X's favorite Field, beating out Forces by a hair. <br /> <br /> (In essence, the idea I'm considering is that most of Prime's Wonder-related capabilities get split between Life and Matter instead of being incorporated into Foundation, with the notable exception of Periapts. Utility would retain nearly all of the Wonder-related capabilities of Primal Utility, with the possible exception of Periapts.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Data:</b> Data, Entropy</u><br /> The Field of Data can do some Correspondence-like things; but while it <i>can</i> be used to locate its subject and to affect him at range, its <i>primary</i> approach to Sympathetic connections has less to do with overcoming distance than it does with working with what the connection <i>means</i>. I'm still working out exactly what that entails, but it's potentially very powerful: consider Nomenclature from <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b> for a sense of how far it might be able to go. Entropy's Ring of Truth and Shape Memes may well be part of this aspect of Data. <br /> <br /> Another aspect of Data involves the ability to interact with computers. This begins with the ability to access the Digital Web, and also interacts with software in a manner that parallels how Mind interacts with a person's cognitive processes. <br /> <br /> Finally, Data might include \u201cstatistics\u201d, i.e. Entropy's chance-based capabilities. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Mind</b></u><br /> I'm thinking of incorporating Bluecho's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/780879-thoughts-on-mind-grades-of-intelligence\">Thoughts on Mind: Grades of Intelligence</a> into the Field of Mind. Otherwise, it parallels the Mind Sphere fairly closely. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Utility</b></u><br /> More or less the same as Primal Utility, possibly without Periapts. Where Foundation specializes in Synergy, Utility deals with Resonance.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> I'm open to criticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-08-2015, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T09:56:35-08:00","id":788169,"title":"","content":"I always liked how a MtAw's (Storyteller Companion I believe) had a section describing the Aracana as Colleges. the same concept could be applied to the Spheres, and could give Technocracy player's an even fancier way of describing themselves. &quot;Alexander Williams, Iteration-X with a PhD from Oxford University in the field of Energy Evolution&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10287-drnevermore","name":"DrNevermore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10287_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T13:57:04-08:00","id":788325,"title":"","content":"I'm very much aware of the \u201cGifted Science\u201d article from MtAw's <b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b>. I'm not particularly fond of overly verbose names, especially for broad topics (in general, I prefer to let the names get longer as the topic gets more focused); thus my current leaning toward single-word names for the Fields. Indeed, my thought here involves something akin to what the Perl 6 programming language community calls \u201cHuffman Encoding\u201d: the length of a thing's name should be inversely related to how frequently used the thing is. Put another way: if you reference it all the time, keep its name short; if you refer to it only occasionally, let its name get longer. <br /> <br /> Speaking of names: since nobody has commented on my proposal to rename what I've been calling \u201cFoundation\u201d as \u201cVoid\u201d, I'm going to go ahead and do it. <br /> <br /> I'm also thinking of taking a page from MtAW's Prime to expand on the ability to manifest blades of raw Primal Energy to a more generalized \u201cenergy constructs\u201d capability: force fields, for instance. Taking that functionality to its extreme would result in something like the \u201cring constructs\u201d made famous (or infamous?) by DC Comics' Green Lantern. Forces would be able to do that, too (remember, I'm OK with some overlap, as long as it doesn't get out of hand); but it might not be quite as adept at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T10:14:44-08:00","id":810672,"title":"","content":"Is there that much left for the Space Sphere to do once Data has been split off on its own? I find Correspondence fairly limited as RAW, and Space in Awakening isn't much better. It has very few applications compared to Forces, Life, or Mind. The vulgar applications are awesome, but it doesn't even control mundane velocity by default.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Data should not just be about digital systems, it should be about any form of network, such as intelligence networks, or converting other Spheres into a topological space. The Spheres don't have a good way of manipulating knowledge itself (Mind deals with memories within individual people, but not facts as abstract metaphysical objects), but the NWO should have a way of examining data about an event and either restricting access to it or altering it. Here's part of my take on Data to illustrate what I mean.<br /> <b>Data 3 \u2013 Facets/Sets, Dimensions</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Data is neither static nor isolated but constantly changing as it interacts with its environment, making it difficult to ever really know where one element ends and another begins. However, Disciples learn to visualize these relationships and quantify even the most vaguely defined concepts.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">By studying a person, the mage can determine how they fit into the world, including details such as profession, income, residence, social contacts, and reputations. Likewise, data about objects can reveal where it was manufactured, what its current value is, or how it might interact with other objects. Combined with other Spheres, the mage can manipulate related sets of data (everyone\u2019s memory of an event, copies of a delivered email) or extract a facet of data and give it independent form (a person\u2019s shadow, bits of luck).<br /> <br /> With their expanded data models, Disciples are also able to conceptualize dimensions beyond the traditional three the human mind can perceive. Though the characteristics of other spatial dimensions are largely based on one\u2019s paradigm and field of study, the ability to temporarily move outside ordinary space allows for feats such as reaching \u201cthrough\u201d solid matter or blinking in and out sight. If the outside region supports extended localization, like the Digital Web does, the mage may transfer things into provided can access an appropriate gateway.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T12:41:18-08:00","id":810746,"title":"","content":"First off: Space keeps the teleportation, colocation, and distance-warping stuff; it picks up much of what the Dimension Science variant Sphere does (save for the \u201csummon/bind/ward entities\u201d stuff, which goes to Void instead); and it governs motion and gravity. If anything, it might be a tad overloaded.<br /> <br /> Your Facets and Sets are fine for Data, but Dimensions is firmly in the purview of Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-17-2016, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T17:39:50-08:00","id":810884,"title":"","content":"Adding motion and gravity helps a lot. Might want to expand on what you can do with space-warping, and not have it all at 5th rank. Personally I see colocation as having very low value, considering its vulgarness and need for Life/Mind to act independently. Another thing you might consider giving it is &quot;pathing&quot; like Lore of Paths from <i>Demon: The Fallen</i>.<br /> <br /> Overall good ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T04:36:40-08:00","id":841820,"title":"","content":"Can I check I'm understanding it right? Five of the spheres are pretty much unchanged (except you're ditching Entropy and reallocating some of it to Time and Data)-<br /> \u2022 Mind<br /> \u2022 Time<br /> \u2022 Forces<br /> \u2022 Life<br /> \u2022 Matter<br /> <br /> The other spheres-<br /> \u2022 Void<br /> \u2022 Space<br /> \u2022 Utility<br /> \u2022 Data<br /> ...mix and match elements of Correspondence, Prime and Spirit in a way that's more suited to the Techno paradigm and overall you're standardising the ranks across spheres as Fields?<br /> <br /> In light of the revisions over the last few months, are you still keeping overlaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9496-barbelith","name":"Barbelith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T11:59:07-08:00","id":842043,"title":"","content":"It's not so much that the first five are largely unchanged as that as of the time of my last post, I hadn't put much thought into how they might be changed. At this point, I'm thinking of maybe replacing Life and Matter with structure and substance, for lack of better terms: structure would deal with the sorts of Effects currently found in Life, but dealing with machines as well as organisms; substance would be more Matter-like, except that it would deal with organic substances (such as wood, oil, ivory, and blood) as well as inorganic ones (minerals, acids, etc.) I'm definitely open to rejiggering the so-called Pattern Spheres so that I don't have to deal with an elephant's tusk differently depending on whether the elephant is alive or dead. <br /> <br /> Forces is more or less technological as written, though a few tweaks may be in order. Frankly, I'd be more inclined to develop a more mystical approach to Forces for the Traditions to use; but that's a topic for another thread. <br /> <br /> I could see Mind taking on a few effects that would Traditionally fall under Spirit \u2014 stuff that deals with what the Traditions might call souls, for instance. <br /> <br /> I would <i>like</i> to standardize the ranks across Fields; it may not be practical to do so, but I'd still like to try. <br /> <br /> As for overlap, I'm not looking for overlap <i>per se</i> so much as I'm looking for parallels that can aid in developing standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:48:46-08:00","id":842196,"title":"","content":"To my mind overlap should be avoided, not only for elegance but because it discourages creative use of conjunctional effects.<br /> <br /> I think you should be bolder with the spheres and make them more mechanically different. RAW Forces does +1 success for damage so it's totally reasonable to write custom spheres with that level of crunchy difference, say Void gives you an extra die when it's used for countermagic purposes, Utility gets additional benefits for group workings, Data gets +1 difficulty for damaging effects, Substance gets +1 success for damage, Structure gets -1 difficulty for transformation... that sort of level of impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9496-barbelith","name":"Barbelith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9496_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T17:40:32-07:00","id":1135641,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Second Draft</u></b><br /> <br /> Nine Fields, organized into three groups:<br /> <br /> Pattern Fields \u2014 Energetics, Materials, Systems<br /> Dynamic Fields \u2014 Space, Time, Void<br /> Abstract Fields \u2014 Data, Mind, Utility<br /> <br /> <i>Energetics</i> deals with light, heat, electricity, and radiation. It's roughly analogous to Forces, with the main difference being that it doesn't cover gravity or motion; that's covered by Space.<br /> <br /> <i>Materials</i> deals with a pattern's composition and physical properties. It's similar to Matter, except that it deals with flesh and bone as well as metals, plastics, stones, etc. And it <i>doesn't</i> deal with machines: if you want to repair an engine or steer a car, you use Systems.<br /> <br /> <i>Systems</i> deals with organisms and mechanisms: essentially, it's Life; but it treats machines as \u201clife forms\u201d after a fashion, letting you communicate with, influence, fix, and break them in much the same way one can communicate with, influence, fix, and break living beings. <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Space</i> incorporates much of Correspondence, except that you can't use it by itself for Sympathetic connections (you need conjunctional use of Data for that) and, as mentioned under Energetics, it deals with gravity and motion as well as space warps. <br /> <br /> <i>Time</i> is largely the same as its equivalent Sphere, with elements of Entropy added in. Specifically, elements related to fate go here. <br /> <br /> <i>Void</i> is one that I'm struggling with. Essentially, it's designed to be used in conjunction with other Fields: pair it with Space to cross the Gauntlet; pair it with Systems to deal with \u201cspirits\u201d; pair it with Energetics to deal with exotic energy sources such as Primal Energy; and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Data</i> and <i>Mind</i> are another pair that I'm not entirely happy with. Data takes over much of the Sympathetic Links stuff from Correspondence, with an emphasis on what a Sympathetic Link <i>means</i>, and what happens when you change a link's meaning. My real problem here is that I'm finding myself wanting to merge Data and Mind, with the combined Field letting you manipulate digital systems in a manner similar to how Mind lets you manipulate people. <br /> <br /> <i>Utility</i> is Primal Utility with the Primal Energy and Tass stuff stripped out. That is, it doesn't do Nodes; but it does Ventures. And it is <i>the</i> Field for creating technological Wonders, save only for Matrices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-30-2017, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T18:38:35-07:00","id":1135650,"title":"","content":"Why not call Void, &quot;Dimension&quot;? So, Primal Energy would be some kind of manipulation of quantum substrate. The rest seems like an easy fit. Space, Time and Dimension don't sound like a bad set.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T20:17:04-07:00","id":1135669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1135641#post1135641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Second Draft</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>Void</i> is one that I'm struggling with. Essentially, it's designed to be used in conjunction with other Fields: pair it with Space to cross the Gauntlet; pair it with Systems to deal with \u201cspirits\u201d; pair it with Energetics to deal with exotic energy sources such as Primal Energy; and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a lot of what it'll influence is what could be described as the more mystical or more farthest frontiers of unknown science. Personally I think the Technocracy would have techniques for manipulating the Consensus, at least in short-term minor ways that could make Paradox harsher or temporarily adjust what is considered vulgar. Even if you don't take that route, it could be the Sphere of Alternate Realities (ie. everything they believe belongs in the Far Umbra).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T02:21:56-07:00","id":1135702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1135641#post1135641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Second Draft</u></b><br /> <br /> Nine Fields, organized into three groups:<br /> <br /> Pattern Fields \u2014 Energetics, Materials, Systems<br /> Dynamic Fields \u2014 Space, Time, Void<br /> Abstract Fields \u2014 Data, Mind, Utility</div> </div> </div> </div>Might I suggest that you allow the Fields to have names consisting of two words, at least? Single word names don't even have a Technocracy vibe to me - they just feel bland and way too limited.<br /> A two word name is certainly not a long one, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-31-2017, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T03:37:26-07:00","id":1135720,"title":"","content":"Only if they have one-word \u201cabbreviations\u201d that get used in practice: e.g., \u201cSpatial Dynamics (Space)\u201d. As I think I mentioned unthread, I see Huffman Encoding playing a part here: the more frequently a thing is used, the shorter its name will be simply it of expedience. I'm reserving the longer names for more specialized Sub-Fields and Procedures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T09:00:49-07:00","id":1135798,"title":"","content":"I'm unclear about Systems. Some of your examples imply that Systems is about higher orders of complexity - e.g., building a car would require Materials and Systems, because Materials on its own can transmute the steel struts and gasoline but can't handle an internal combustion engine. Other examples don't - e.g., you propose that Mind (or combined Data/Mind) is sufficient for all orders of complexity on mental systems.<br /> <br /> If you want the former case to take prominence, then Systems becomes too important. Other fields are fine for low-level stuff - e.g., Mind 2 to push an emotion into someone's mind - but Systems is required for all the 4-dot or 5-dot type stuff that's more complex, to a point that other fields become something like a vidare for Spirit - the &quot;flavor&quot; or &quot;direction&quot; of the Systems field. <br /> <br /> If you want the latter case, then it's hard to see a place for Systems at all. It feels like the &quot;weakness/breaking things&quot; part of Entropy except you can strengthen/repair things too. And like Entropy, it steps on everyone else's toes. Also, if you return the &quot;complexity&quot; to the other fields, they can become too powerful; Materials would then basically be both Life and Matter for the price of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T12:16:19-07:00","id":1135865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1135720#post1135720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if they have one-word \u201cabbreviations\u201d that get used in practice: e.g., \u201cSpatial Dynamics (Space)\u201d. As I think I mentioned unthread, I see Huffman Encoding playing a part here: the more frequently a thing is used, the shorter its name will be simply it of expedience. I'm reserving the longer names for more specialized Sub-Fields and Procedures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the names adjusted into adjectival forms when combined?<br /> <br /> Time Systems or Temporal Systems?<br /> Space Data or Spatial Analytics?<br /> Void(Dimension?) Utility or Dimensional Utility?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T13:17:02-07:00","id":1135899,"title":"","content":"Dimensional Utility sounds very good. Combining the concepts of Utility and Value with the Anthropic Principle to be the judge the value of that which lies beyond human experience. Perhaps with this combinations you can do Nodes, including the famous sanitization.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Data</i> and <i>Mind</i> are another pair that I'm not entirely happy with. Data takes over much of the Sympathetic Links stuff from Correspondence, with an emphasis on what a Sympathetic Link <i>means</i>, and what happens when you change a link's meaning. My real problem here is that I'm finding myself wanting to merge Data and Mind, with the combined Field letting you manipulate digital systems in a manner similar to how Mind lets you manipulate people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could merge Data and Mind. Space already takes the thunder of Data by allowing teleportation, co-location and such...The Mind could be conceived as the software of the body, and thus be under the general Field of Data that covers from the humble, but meaningfull, byte of data to the AI and the natural inteligence . Also, the idea that thoughts are tied to concepts like sympathy works very well for the Technocracy, as ties to the concepts of hive-minds and society (the system) dictating individual tought. As 1984 would put it: <i>Reality it's in the mind, not in the mind of the Individual, that's mortal and fallible, but in the mind of the Party that's collective and eternal</i> . It wouldn't allow for anything like Astral Travel alone, unless it's through the Web","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-31-2017, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T16:55:03-07:00","id":1135999,"title":"","content":"I think/interpolate that the difference between Data and Mind might be along the linds of Data= Information (which can be in books, on computers, in people's heads) and Mind = Psychology/Sociology/Anthropology typically in a very Applied manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T05:21:22-07:00","id":1154097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1135999#post1135999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think/interpolate that the difference between Data and Mind might be along the linds of Data= Information (which can be in books, on computers, in people's heads) and Mind = Psychology/Sociology/Anthropology typically in a very Applied manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that the difference between Correspondence: Data and the Technocracy's Mind is that Correspondence: Data deals with space, while the Technocracy's Mind deals with manipulating and influencing persons. I don't think those two could be merged in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T09:28:06-07:00","id":1154138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1154097#post1154097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that the difference between Correspondence: Data and the Technocracy's Mind is that Correspondence: Data deals with space, while the Technocracy's Mind deals with manipulating and influencing persons. I don't think those two could be merged in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Data as written is just Corespondence re-skinned so that the Laws of Contagion and Association deal strictly with modern information as opposed to the typical more esoteric conceptions. If the real difference is that your True Name is now your SSID and the whole thing is about teleporting still, it's not really about Data. <br /> <br /> Since this is about changing the status quo, I'm thinking Data in RAW is pretty much a wash. It's really just a Foci concern. Of course, the Technocracy finds people using modern information. What has that got to do with space manipulation? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T10:36:27-07:00","id":1154162,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Data, in the context of this project, has little to do with space; manipulating Space is covered by, well, Space. The closest that Data gets to transcending space is that it is the Field used to access the Digital Web; and the Digital Web transcends space. <br /> <br /> For the most part, the Sympathetic aspects of Data are less about transcending distance than they're about identifying and utilizing (and sometimes establishing or eliminating) similarities between two things. You <i>can</i> still do the sorts of things that the Traditions can do with Correspondence; but that frequently requires conjunctional use of Data and Space. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Data lets you alter records (including written records), mess with software, spoof sensors, and otherwise make a nuisance of yourself where information systems are concerned. A lot of this echoes what the Sphere of Mind does with respect to people, which when combined to Iteration X's views on cybernetics (and my proposed replacement of Matter and Life with Materials and Systems) made me wonder where (or even <i>if</i>) the line should be drawn between the Fields of Data and Mind. <br /> <br /> Another example of potential overlap: translations. If Mind and Data are distinct Fields, should the ability to understand something written in a foreign language be covered by Mind or by Data?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T10:49:17-07:00","id":1154164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1135798#post1135798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unclear about Systems. Some of your examples imply that Systems is about higher orders of complexity - e.g., building a car would require Materials and Systems, because Materials on its own can transmute the steel struts and gasoline but can't handle an internal combustion engine. Other examples don't - e.g., you propose that Mind (or combined Data/Mind) is sufficient for all orders of complexity on mental systems.<br /> <br /> If you want the former case to take prominence, then Systems becomes too important. Other fields are fine for low-level stuff - e.g., Mind 2 to push an emotion into someone's mind - but Systems is required for all the 4-dot or 5-dot type stuff that's more complex, to a point that other fields become something like a vidare for Spirit - the &amp;quot;flavor&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;direction&amp;quot; of the Systems field. <br /> <br /> If you want the latter case, then it's hard to see a place for Systems at all. It feels like the &amp;quot;weakness/breaking things&amp;quot; part of Entropy except you can strengthen/repair things too. And like Entropy, it steps on everyone else's toes. Also, if you return the &amp;quot;complexity&amp;quot; to the other fields, they can become too powerful; Materials would then basically be both Life and Matter for the price of one.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main thought here was to take the phenomena normally covered by Life and Matter and to shift the dividing line from \u201cliving or not\u201d to \u201cstructure or composition\u201d. My main concern here is that this potentially messes with the Progenitors, whose views tend to focus heavily on, well, life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T15:37:09-07:00","id":1154528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1154162#post1154162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Data, in the context of this project, has little to do with space; manipulating Space is covered by, well, Space. The closest that Data gets to transcending space is that it is the Field used to access the Digital Web; and the Digital Web transcends space.<br /> <br /> For the most part, the Sympathetic aspects of Data are less about transcending distance than they're about identifying and utilizing (and sometimes establishing or eliminating) similarities between two things. You <i>can</i> still do the sorts of things that the Traditions can do with Correspondence; but that frequently requires conjunctional use of Data and Space.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Data lets you alter records (including written records), mess with software, spoof sensors, and otherwise make a nuisance of yourself where information systems are concerned. A lot of this echoes what the Sphere of Mind does with respect to people, which when combined to Iteration X's views on cybernetics (and my proposed replacement of Matter and Life with Materials and Systems) made me wonder where (or even <i>if</i>) the line should be drawn between the Fields of Data and Mind.<br /> <br /> Another example of potential overlap: translations. If Mind and Data are distinct Fields, should the ability to understand something written in a foreign language be covered by Mind or by Data?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends.... Is Data all about information? (Which seems.... apt.) Then linguistics is just coding. So, Data would do it. In which case Mind has to do something else. But since Mind is psychology, then it's all the mind control, telepathy, etc. Applied psychology and sociology. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T07:23:30-07:00","id":1154701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1154528#post1154528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends.... Is Data all about information? (Which seems.... apt.) Then linguistics is just coding. So, Data would do it. In which case Mind has to do something else. But since Mind is psychology, then it's all the mind control, telepathy, etc. Applied psychology and sociology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telepathy it's not that different from language. You're just transmiting information using a non physical medium, you're bypassing ears and eyes and getting right into the brain...no need of psychology to do that. Maybe Data + Systems to bypass the ears/eyes?<br /> <br /> Mind control of some sort may also be doable by manipulating the information on the brain. What you see, what you hear, all that influence your mind. So does your memory, which according to some (very technocratical) theories may as well be just data stored in a biological medium. Arguably mass media controls your mind by controling what information you can access. Psychology it's necessary to determine the effect, but to what extent?, many manipulative persons do this sort of stuff almost instinctively.<br /> <br /> Some theories treat the mind and society as systems (in one case biological and in the other...well, social) The problem it's that I don't like to add Systems to anything else because that Field it's already bloated as it is, doing little on it's own, but being THE Field to use in conjunctions. Mind, or something similar to Mind, may be useful to deflate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-01-2017, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T07:58:11-07:00","id":1154711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1154701#post1154701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Telepathy it's not that different from language. You're just transmiting information using a non physical medium, you're bypassing ears and eyes and getting right into the brain...no need of psychology to do that. Maybe Data + Systems to bypass the ears/eyes?<br /> <br /> Mind control of some sort may also be doable by manipulating the information on the brain. What you see, what you hear, all that influence your mind. So does your memory, which according to some (very technocratical) theories may as well be just data stored in a biological medium. Arguably mass media controls your mind by controling what information you can access. Psychology it's necessary to determine the effect, but to what extent?, many manipulative persons do this sort of stuff almost instinctively.<br /> <br /> Some theories treat the mind and society as systems (in one case biological and in the other...well, social) The problem it's that I don't like to add Systems to anything else because that Field it's already bloated as it is, doing little on it's own, but being THE Field to use in conjunctions. Mind, or something similar to Mind, may be useful to deflate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telepathy is very different from language in methodology. The medium is not the message. Spheres typically allow you to do things that are otherwise impossible or, alternatively, to do possible things in impossible ways or to an impossible degree. Otherwise it would take a Mage with Matter 2 to make toast. Telepathy is doing a fairly normal thing (&quot;listening&quot; or &quot;talking&quot;) but doing it by bypassing the normal/Consesus-approved way of doing so. If you could understand someone when they talked to you, then using Mind allows you to do all that without talking or listening. (The &quot;How&quot; of that is the Focus, which would be various kinds of pyschology, or neurology or kinesics/proxemics or whatever way your particular Technocrat swings.) So you NEED Mind to do that telepathy thing. Or to use mind control. Mind/Data would come in if you wanted to sift or edit the information in the mind in question. You'd still need Data/Mind to do that even if, say, your Progenitor was doing some weird neuro-electrical phreaking brain hack by pointing some doo-dad at the target's head, as Spheres are about WHAT you want to do and Foci are about HOW you do it. Otherwise you are getting into massive Sphere bloat and keeping players from being able to use their character's magic to do things in what will be ultimately be a semi-arbitrary fashion.<br /> <br /> Which is why mind control is not manipulating information in the brain on the Sphere end. That may be HOW you do it, but it is not what you are doing. Data is going to be able to access and manipulate information in ANY media, human thoughts, books, computer drives, media, etc. Though some of those are going to take additional Fields/Spheres depending on how they are accessed. And sometimes other Fields/Spheres should make certain effects much easier. (E.g. if the Progenitor had Systems, Biology and/or Space as well, it would be much easier to do what they are trying to do and be able to do so in different ways, but all it takes do effect is Data/Mind.) <br /> <br /> If brains are just information, then, well, EVERYTHING is just information. Physics, Biology, Systems, Space, Time... they all take an observer who is collecting and processing information. That sounds like a great Focus, but it doesn't sound like good mechanics. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T08:48:43-07:00","id":1154726,"title":"","content":"I think I kinda get your argument, but I don't understand it entirely:<br /> <br /> You say Data can access information on any medium, including the mind...But yet somehow that's not mind reading telepathy?. Are you saying that Data CAN'T access the mind without Mind because the medium it's Mind based? or that Mind wouldn't need Data to access the mind because the message itself it's mundane and thus you don't need the Information sphere to get it unless it's in another language?. Matter can make a toast, so can Forces + existing energy + Bread. These overlaps aren't always bad, but boundaries need to be placed. I don't quite get where do you want to place the boundaries.<br /> <br /> Also, implying that I said that everything it's information just because I argued that a human mind may act like a computer and that society can be understood as a system (not Data, but the other &quot;problem sphere&quot;) it's a bit misleading. If you can acces and manipulate a computer with Data instead of Forces, why can't you do the same with the Mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-01-2017, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:16:50-07:00","id":1154777,"title":"","content":"About the only aspect of Mind that I don't see readily implemented in Data is the emotional component.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T18:38:08-07:00","id":1154923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy?p=1154777#post1154777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the only aspect of Mind that I don't see readily implemented in Data is the emotional component.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then just say emotions are biological.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:33:25-07:00","id":1154938,"title":"","content":"Perhaps. I <i>am</i> thinking that some of these Fields (particularly the more broad ones) might require you to choose a mandatory specialty, a bit like the way some versions of the Storyteller/ing System requires you to focus the scope of the likes of Science and Academics. I think that might make Systems a bit more palatable, by making it less like an \u00fcber-Sphere. The Progenitors could then focus on Biological Systems and Biological Materials, while Iteration X might have members who deal specifically with Cybernetic Systems (which would only apply to Patterns that mix biological and mechanical components), etc. <br /> <br /> In this view, I might fold all of the Data stuff into Mind, and require a specialty in terms of what sort of \u201cmind\u201d you're dealing with. The default would be human minds; but Iteration X could instead specialize in digital \u201cminds\u201d (i.e., \u201cData\u201d), Progenitors might sometimes specialize in animal \u201cminds\u201d (a specialty not geared toward dealing with \u201chigher cognitive functions\u201d, but quite capable of messing with emotions, instincts, and the like), and some Void Engineers might specialize in Exopsychology (i.e., getting into the heads of Umbral Entities). <br /> <br /> The idea is that nobody would be able to do it all, at least not without making a concerted effort to develop multiple specialties, and that some \u201cFields\u201d don't represent single areas of understanding so much as they represent sets of similar Fields \u2014 similar in the sense of \u201cthey can do similar things\u201d, distinct in the sense of \u201cthey affect different kinds of things\u201d. <br /> <br /> Subfields would be like these mandatory specialties, but optional: if you want someone who concentrates on learning all about light to the exclusion of heat, electricity, radiation, etc., you could have him learn a subfield of Energetics that specializes in Light. It would be easier to learn, but more limited in what it could do. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T07:13:21-07:00","id":1155044,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of folding Data into Mind, and then allow it to affect computers w/o &quot;Energetics&quot; and create sympathetic connections. Data wasn't doing much on it's own, Mind was, it makes sense to fold the small into the big.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, well...<br /> <br /> The way you put it resembles a little to Ars Magica system where you need to combine two words (In ars case it was a verb and a sustantive) to get a spell. However, Speciality works by partitioning the scope of the Field instead of combining the two words into something bigger, and this makes me question it's utility in this case:<br /> Speciality system works with Science and other skills because listing all possible sciences would take a lot of space on the sheet, however, if you have a character that's a chemist, you can describe it as a &quot;Chemist&quot; , you don't need to tell other players that he's a &quot;scientist with a focus on chemistry&quot; because that's a given.<br /> <br /> Major Fields become bags of fields. The problem that I see it's that you could easily ignore the bag and merely have a huge system of cheap sub-fields. Systems wouldn't do any good: I could easily say &quot;I know Materials&quot;/&quot;I know Biologicals&quot; and everyone would undestand I'm a &quot;systems user&quot;. Systems becomes more like Arete than a Sphere.<br /> <br /> I'm intrigued by this idea of combining two words, but I don't have a clue on how to make it work (other than Ars managed to do something like it. I.E: By breaking &quot;Creation Sphere&quot; into what can you create: animals, fire, water, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T13:41:40-07:00","id":1155180,"title":"","content":"\u201cPartitioning the scope of the Field\u201d is a pretty good way of putting it. From my example, some of the possible partitions might include:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Mind:</b> <i>human</i>, animal, digital, alien<br /> \u2022 <b>Systems:</b> biological, mechanical, cybernetic<br /> \u2022 <b>Materials:</b> organic, inorganic<br /> <br /> Remember, this is a work in progress; at the moment, I'm still developing my thoughts on this partitioning mechanism. Some thoughts, though:<br /> <br /> 1. Mandatory partitions wouldn't be cheaper than whole Fields \u2014 at least, the first one wouldn't be; whether additional ones would get a price break is an open question. By contrast, optional partitions (Subfields) would definitely be cheaper than whole Fields; but I'm not sure how much cheaper. <br /> <br /> 2. There have been complaints that my naming convention is too bland. I responded with a line about Huffman Encoding: common-use things get concise names; more specific, less common things get more elaborate names. More importantly, more elaborate names are there for a reason, not merely fancy for the sake of being fancy. Adding an adjective when you apply a partition is an application of this principle, as it gives you a standardized way to refer to the Fields and their partitions. Assigning a concise name to a particular partition of a Field that sees a lot of use (e.g., referring to \u201cDigital Mind\u201d as \u201cData\u201d) is another example of this principle in action.<br /> <br /> 3. There have been complaints that Systems is too broad, and too close to being a \u201cdo anything\u201d Sphere. Partitions are an attempt to address that: you should never be able to take dots in just \u201cSystems\u201d; you should be required to specify what <i>type</i> of Systems you're studying. My initial inclination is that each mandatory partition would get its own dot rating; but again, that's something that's still under development.<br /> <br /> 4. So why go with \u201cFields with required partitions\u201d instead of sets of Fields? For one thing, it cuts down on redundant Effects lists. Systems generalizes the Life Sphere, providing Effects akin to healing/harming/transformative magick in a way that can apply to things other than living organisms. You can recover Life from this by applying a Biological partition to Systems; but you can also establish what would amount to a Machine Sphere by applying a Mechanical partition to it. In both cases, you have the same list of Effects to work off of; the only difference is that one of the partitions deals with organisms while the other deals with mechanisms.<br /> <br /> 5. Another reason to go with partitioned Fields is that the list of partitions is potentially open-ended. Do you want to try a Weather Systems partition? I can't guarantee that it would work; it's well beyond the scope that Systems was originally conceived to address. But give it a try. There's something to be said for encouraging creativity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:27:16-07:00","id":1155405,"title":"","content":"Quite interesting. Mechanically it seems a bit like vampire system, where you have a &quot;primary path&quot; that's increased at Discipline cost, and then you can have &quot;secondary paths&quot;. Of course, there's a lot of differences. The major Fields aren't just a bag but actually have things that they do that are common to all subfields (As I understand it, Systems works as Life but with a broader interpretation of what constitutes a live subject). <br /> <br /> Materials could also include a &quot;Extradimensional&quot; subfield, to control lifeless Ephemera.<br /> <br /> You may even put Time/Space and whatever parts of &quot;Spirit&quot; that wasn't delved into Systems, as different partitions of a unified Field of Dimensions. Dimensions would deal with scrying, travel, distances, areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T20:27:58-08:00","id":1156559,"title":"","content":"It's tempting. My main concern is that Space deviates from this a bit: first, it also incorporates motion and gravity, as part of making it the Field of travel. Second, it <i>doesn't</i> use the standard Correspondence chart for teleports and portals; if you want to do that sort of thing, you bring in conjunctional Data. <b>Revised Void Engineers Convention Book</b> has a \u201cVoid Correspondence\u201d chart that's conceptually right for Space; but its implementation worries me as being too open to abuse. <br /> <br /> Time, too, has things in it other than temporal scrying and time travel. There's the ability to adjust the flow of time; and whatever Entropy-like Effects don't end up in Data end up in Time.<br /> <br /> Now, I did say that various partitions of a Field do <i>similar</i> things, allowing for some differences based on the subject matter. But I was thinking in terms of how Data (i.e., Digital Mind) wouldn't have anything empathy-like, whereas \u201cAnimal Mind\u201d wouldn't have much if anything involving thoughts; or how Biological Systems would have procedures for directing the healing process that Mechanical Systems would lack. I'm not sure that the added stuff that Space and Time have would fall under the \u201csimilar\u201d category. It's more like Space, Time, and Void all have a thread of similar Effects centered around remote access (where each defines \u201cremote\u201d differently) in addition to the other things they do. Heck, Data also partakes of that thread, with the Digital Web being at the heart of its concept of \u201cremote\u201d. <br /> <br /> There's something to be said for that sort of \u201ccode reuse\u201d; but I'm not sure that partitioned Fields are the best way to handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}